# cPanel publish channel — configuration reference.
#
# NOTHING here is read from a file at runtime. These names exist as GitHub
# Actions **secrets on the PROD environment**, and as two one-line files on the
# host. This template documents them; it never carries a value.

# ── GitHub Actions secrets (environment: PROD) ───────────────────────────────
# The FTPS host is NOT the cPanel API host and NOT the public domain:
#   cPanel API  → business138.web-hosting.com:2083   (account mascehgw)
#   FTPS        → business138.web-hosting.com        (origin 66.29.132.45)
# FTP cannot traverse Cloudflare, so this must always be the origin hostname.
#
# Changed 2026-07-28: the landing moved off the shared account `anakxipn`
# (premium224, 66.29.146.21) onto the dedicated `mascehgw`, which it shares only
# with bowerfans PROD. The shared account was at 184,625 of 300,000 inodes with
# LVE peaks of 1.92 of 2 GiB; this one started at 3,134 of 600,000.
CPANEL_FTP_HOST=business138.web-hosting.com

# FTP account chrooted to this docroot only. One account per environment, so a
# compromised QA credential cannot write to the landing.
CPANEL_FTP_USER=
CPANEL_FTP_PASS=

# ── Files on the host, one per docroot ───────────────────────────────────────
# /home/<account>/1platform.pro/.deploy/.health_url
#   https://1platform.pro/
# /home/<account>/1platform.pro/.deploy/.health_marker
#   One string that only OUR page contains. A bare 200 proves nothing: this
#   shared origin answers 200 with a 163-byte default page to any unknown Host.
#
# Both files are per-docroot on purpose: more than one docroot shares this cPanel
# account (bowerfans PROD lives here too), and a hardcoded default would let one
# site's cron read another's health signal and roll back on it.
#
# `.health_url` is seeded only AFTER this host has been cut over. Before that the
# public URL is answered by the legacy origin, so a health check here would grade
# the other channel — and `activate.sh` treats a missing file as "skip", never as
# "guess".

# ── Optional overrides for activate.sh (defaults are fine) ───────────────────
# CPANEL_KEEP_RELEASES=2
# CPANEL_HEALTH_RETRIES=6
# CPANEL_HEALTH_SLEEP=5
